From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anothers <14343424+Anothers@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 95/95] dsv41: route head/engram/dspark onto dense3 and fuse r1
 DSpark passes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extract shared Emitter.dense3Eligible(k, n, k2) and route the remaining
r1 dense EXL3 projections — LM head (K2=12), prefill engram.wkv (K2=10),
and dspark.main_proj (K2=8, chunked at dense.rows_max during ingest) —
onto dense3 (lanes), eliminating all 7 legacy linear_v4 calls per decode
window at zero extra memory under TF_DSV41_FORMS_INPLACE=1.

Align DSpark's r1 pass with backbone fusions: mhcInto(..., .boundary,
false) (non-aliasing spare streams to avoid #2715 cross-CTA races),
fusedNorm q_norm, qrope=1 (ATTN_ROPE), woFold (gated by rot_fold & 1),
and direct bf16 TP exchanges in dspark_gpu_device.zig and
dspark_slots_device.zig. Adds host tests in block_test.zig verifying
x != xout on every boundary mhc_cuda call in emitPass and n=200 ingest
chunking.
